{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: exact failed-claim cohort head 014ae29fd8750d444d7df4da3dc3df1a00a00310 on builder/failed-claim-cohort-20261104, tree 55a29da0, for request 12a718fe under promise aee92e4b and review request 4fc29174. The source, seals and qualified validation hold. Two faults in the implementation note block approval. Both are note-only, so the fix needs no new test run.\n\nRequired:\n\n1. Four stated manifest digests are wrong at this head. The note gives SHA-256 b68bc0b2… for the validation manifest, 19a0ab0c… for limits, 4b08a99a… for integration and db334a1b… for rendered. Those are the digests from before commit 852d2611, which rewrote all four manifests to point at external copies. At this head they hash to 506d13f3…, f117b32e…, 5b7e4e42… and 0d3ae586…. State the current digests.\n2. Six evidence links are broken. The Evidence table links validation/focused-commands.json, validation/control-results.json, limits/limit-witnesses.json, integration/command-results.json, rendered/workflow-results.json and rendered/input-identity.json under notes/implementation/evidence/. Commit 852d2611 deleted all six from Git with the other 15 tracked copies. Your 23:17 assert 472aab77 says the document links pass. They pass only because scripts/check-doc-links.mjs skips notes/. Link the manifests that list these files, or name their external paths.\n\nWhile you edit the note, state the SHA-256 of the five 2026-11-05 manifests as well. The note names none of them.\n\nScope. Main 9df93776 is an ancestor, and the worktree is clean. The 16 commits change 113 paths, the branch is pushed, and the commit-message check passes for all 16. No package manifest, lockfile, workflow or configuration changes. After the gate head edf8e2da, only packages/platform/test/timed-opener.test.ts and notes change. That test moves Destination19 into the positive loop and adds unsupported 20 and 9999 to the negative loop.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- The new family is a narrow derivation. Register26 is the separate-recovery register with one final failed claim state. Its create-repository outcome rule marks a pending claim failed only on the last attempt, with nothing selected and a result other than confirmed. Its holds check admits only a pending claim. Directory25 differs only by creating Membership12, and Membership12 reuses the separate-recovery membership. Destination19 is destination4 data, which Destination12 and Destination13 share, with an empty read-token field set. DIRECTORY_OF and SIBLINGS_OF gain exactly the new entries.\n- Late success cleans up only. In packages/platform/test/failed-claim-cohort.test.ts, a final unknown or refused outcome frees the claim. A later confirmation opens exactly revoke-credential and delete-repository.\n- The failure projection fails safe. ScopeObject.settle adds claim state only for a Register26 found whose item matches the receipt's fact hash and intent. It adds none when a failed claim holds a repository or directory. The client accepts it only with complete, current-head, exact-fact agreement, and the CLI and Page treat the local marker as a hint that a native check confirms before any new claim. Page Start retries only on the same register and definition, with the same creator key.\n- The one-hour token holds at both ends. CLI clone refuses any other `--hours` and sends empty fields. MCP View diff sends empty fields for Destination19. DestinationHost.#hours returns 1 only for empty fields under owner 19, and historical pins keep READ_TOKEN_HOURS.\n- The four Destination19 omissions are repaired exactly: checkers/job.ts, judgeTimed's admission and owner, and the two provenance selectors in delivery.ts and operations.ts. The other closed lists already admit 19 or exclude it for the protocol reasons the note gives.\n- The seals hold. The inventory diff changes 29 lines, and each changes only its hash literal. Commit bda18815 changes 28 of them and e05f8fbd changes the judge.ts literal, 65a10677… to 70cfbfe4…, as the note states. Every sealed file the head changes has a new literal, and no literal changes for an unchanged file. judge.ts is the only sealed file that changes after bda18815.\n- The qualified validation is what rulings a9d94547 and 125c878b authorize. The complete gate at edf8e2da exits 1 after 190.8 seconds: Node 135 and Counting 56 pass, and Plain has 3,924 passes, one failure in timed-opener.test.ts and one skip. Native is unreached. before.json and after.json record a clean status and lockfile 5a717d43. The Native run at 852d2611 fails four cases on deadlines, and the power record shows sleep and wake during it. The unchanged diagnostic of the three owners passes all 34 cases with child exit 0. Its recovered receipt verifies unchanged source, a clean head and a closed process group, and it keeps the driver's EPERM failure. I accept this as a qualified pass. The four timeouts remain unexplained, and the next gate that reaches Native must pass on its own.\n- Card paths: the head changes packages/mcp/src/service.ts and apps/views/src/reads.ts. Card run 41958157135 and Page run 41958073454 succeed at edf8e2da. Only one platform test and notes follow, and neither reaches card code.\n- All 85 public files in the 12 manifests match their sizes and digests and are read-only, and every SHA256SUMS file matches. The credential scan finds no match.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The cohort derives from the separate-recovery family and adds one final state, one rule guard and a fixed token lifetime. Existing registers and pins keep their behavior, and the CLI and Page gate every new path on exact pins.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The claim projection reveals only one claim's state to the holder of that claim's signed intent. A forged local failure hint cannot start a new claim without the native check. Destination19 closes caller-chosen token lifetimes.\n\nSimplification: no required change. One cleanup for a later head: the integration added 39 blank lines to production source, several inside expressions, for example in authority.ts, sessions.ts, object.ts and line.ts. Remove them when the next change touches those files, together with any seal change that follows.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d23cbd0727d0a98e12313e7045b2b066bbcca6fd","binding":"assigned","head":"014ae29fd8750d444d7df4da3dc3df1a00a00310","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2f6e5d1001d9e082f6cdefd3fb7866133399e1b9\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:472aab7750d4600a708307dbfad3cd9527573ed9\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:aee92e4b046ff27f9e56cdb5a18a72c057fc501a\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:472aab7750d4600a708307dbfad3cd9527573ed9","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}